      <p>Prepare the folder for the guide. At the end of this lesson, the <code>my-audacity-guide</code> folder contains an empty <code>topics</code> folder, where the topics of later lessons go.</p>
      <p><strong>Time:</strong> about 5 minutes. <strong>You need:</strong> the DogsBay XML editor, and the empty <code>my-audacity-guide</code> folder open in it. See <a href="/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/start-here/set-up">Set up your tools</a>.</p>
      <h2 id="step-1-create-the-topics-folder" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 1: Create the topics folder<a href="#step-1-create-the-topics-folder" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>A DITA project is a folder of topics and maps. Maps stay in the project folder, and topics go in a folder of their own, so that the project stays readable as it grows.</p>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create the folder</strong> In the <strong>Explorer</strong>, right-click <code>my-audacity-guide</code> and choose <strong>New Folder</strong>. Type <code>topics</code> and press Enter.
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Confirm the result</strong> The <strong>Explorer</strong> shows <code>topics</code> inside <code>my-audacity-guide</code>.
      </Step>
      </Steps>
